{
  "an7.42:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.42 ",
  "an7.42:0.2": "4. Deities ",
  "an7.42:0.3": "Graduation (1st) ",
  "an7.42:1.1": "Then Venerable Sāriputta robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Sāvatthī for alms. ",
  "an7.42:1.2": "Then it occurred to him, ",
  "an7.42:1.3": "“It’s too early to wander for alms in Sāvatthī. ",
  "an7.42:1.4": "Why don’t I visit the monastery for the wanderers of other religions?” ",
  "an7.42:1.5": "Then he went to the monastery for the wanderers of other religions and exchanged greetings with the wanderers there. ",
  "an7.42:1.6": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side. ",
  "an7.42:1.7": "Now at that time while those wanderers of other religions were sitting together this discussion came up among them, ",
  "an7.42:1.8": "“Reverends, anyone who lives the full and pure spiritual life for twelve years is qualified to be called a ‘graduate mendicant’.” ",
  "an7.42:2.1": "Sāriputta neither approved nor rejected that statement of the wanderers of other religions. ",
  "an7.42:2.2": "He rose from his seat, thinking, ",
  "an7.42:2.3": "“I will learn the meaning of this statement from the Buddha himself.” ",
  "an7.42:2.4": "Then Sāriputta wandered for alms in Sāvatthī. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and told him what had happened, adding: ",
  "an7.42:3.1": "",
  "an7.42:3.2": "",
  "an7.42:3.3": "",
  "an7.42:3.4": "",
